  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I: During Electrolytic refining, the pure metal is made to act as anode and its impure metallic form is used as cathode.<br />Statement II: During the Hall-Heroult electrolysis process, purified <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is mixed with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>AlF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;to lower the melting point of the mixture.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HWLkV",
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct",
      "isCorrect": true,
